\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The evidence in favor of Jehoahaz is fairly strong, and there are no other good candidates who match what Ezekiel says about the first cub.\
You appear to have left out a king of Judah in the succession though. Jehoiakim "did what was evil in the sight of the Lord, according to all that his fathers had done" according to 2 Kings 23:37. He "filled Jerusalem with innocent blood" according to 2 Kings 24:4. This is given as the reason that the LORD sent bands from four nations to destroy Judah. Daniel 1:2 says the LORD gave him into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar. 2 Chronicles 6:6 says Nebuchadnezzar bound him in chains to take him to Babylon. Admittedly, it is not entirely clear if he survived for long enough to reach Babylon. He was the next in the line of succession, making the most sense out of Ezekiel 19:5, "When she saw that she waited in vain,\'a0that her hope was lost,she took another of her cubs\'a0and made him a young lion." That is, Jehoiakim was the king who was made king in the wake of Jehoahaz clearly not coming back. Lastly, and this is weaker evidence, the taxation mentioned in 2 Kings 23:33-35 may be one of the reasons for the description of laying waste cities - though the raids by the nations as the LORD's response to his bloodshed may instead be what is referred to there.\
As evidence against, he was not a son of the same mother as Jehoahaz - though this is less of a problem to the degree we interpret the mother lion as the house of David or the house of Judah. His death happened some time before this lament would have been written, and similarly, the rule of the Davidic monarchy in Judah did not end with him. \
As evidence to be considered for any of these candidates, there is the tie between the discussion of the monarchy in chapter 19 and the discussion in chapters 18 and 17.\
How do you view the connections between these chapters, and how do you sum up all the evidence for each candidate for the second cub?
\f0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
