God's purposes and character to bring forward:
\b0 \cf2 \
The divine intolerance for corrupted holy things stands out most starkly. God would rather have no Davidic king than one who devours his people. This isn't petulance but protective love - corrupted authority claiming divine backing does more damage than honest paganism. He'll make His own promises appear to fail rather than let them shelter predation.\
The precision of consequences matters. The fire comes from the branch that misused authority. The nations respond to the roaring they heard. God's judgment isn't arbitrary but emergence of what was already present - He lets things become what they truly are, then ensures recognition of what that is.\
His commitment to reality over appearance. The vine was planted by abundant waters (divine blessing) but this very blessing became the height that ensured visible destruction. God won't maintain appearances of covenant faithfulness when the reality has been hollowed out.\

